<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pact of Zanjón</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1878</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ten-years-war">Ten Years' War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Pact of Zanjón was the agreement of 10 February 1878 that ended most of the fighting in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ten-years-war">Ten Years' War</a> between Cuban rebels and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>. Negotiated with General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arsenio-martinez-campos">Arsenio Martínez Campos</a>, it granted an amnesty and freed slaves and Chinese indentured workers who had fought with the rebels, but brought neither independence nor general abolition. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antonio-maceo">Antonio Maceo</a> rejected it in the Protest of Baraguá.</p></div>
